Levels and Subtrees in a Binary Tree

Tree Diagram

		     15
		   /    \
		 35      12
		/  \
	     3    6
	    / \  / \
	   1  10 5   7

Levels in This Tree

Level 0: 15
Level 1: 35, 12
Level 2: 3, 6
Level 3: 1, 10, 5, 7

Note:
- Root node is always at level 0.
- Level of a node = number of edges from root to that node.

Subtrees in This Tree

1) Subtree rooted at 35:

	    35
	   /
	  3
	 / \
	1  10

2) Subtree rooted at 6:

	  6
	 / \
	5   7

3) Subtree rooted at 12:

	12

Important Point:
Every node itself can be considered a subtree root.
So, each node in a tree forms one subtree with all of its descendants.
